Applied by ../prep.common to upstream's src/scanner.c on every regen.
Regen fails if this patch no longer applies. If upstream has fixed the bug,
delete this file.

SECENG-77: the serializer loop checks `size < BUFFER_SIZE` but writes two
bytes per step. With an odd number of open string delimiters and enough
indent levels, it writes one byte past the 1024-byte state buffer.
Upstream tree-sitter-python master still has this bug.

--- a/scanner.c
+++ b/scanner.c
@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@
     size += delimiter_count;
 
     uint32_t iter = 1;
-    for (; iter < scanner->indents.size && size < TREE_SITTER_SERIALIZATION_BUFFER_SIZE; ++iter) {
+    for (; iter < scanner->indents.size && size + 1 < TREE_SITTER_SERIALIZATION_BUFFER_SIZE; ++iter) {
         uint16_t indent_value = *array_get(&scanner->indents, iter);
         buffer[size++] = (char)(indent_value & 0xFF);
         buffer[size++] = (char)((indent_value >> 8) & 0xFF);
